REGIONAL REGULATION OF HULU SUNGAI UTARA REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2016

CONCERNING

THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF HULU SUNGAI UTARA,

Considering:

a. that in the context of protecting the rights of women and children as mandated by the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, improving the quality of life of women and children and addressing all forms of violence against women and children, there is a need for concern from all parties, both the community and related government institutions and law enforcement officials;
b. that there is a tendency of increasing victims and cases of violence against women and children, which have not been handled optimally, thus requiring integrated services by relevant agencies and community institutions/organizations to provide protection for women and children victims of violence;
c. that in an effort to facilitate women and children to improve their skills and independence and to obtain consultation services and solutions to problems experienced by women and children, there is a need for an integrated service center for the empowerment of women and children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;

In View of:

1. Law Number 27 of 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Law Number 3 Drt. of 1953 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Kalimantan (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1953 Number 9, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2756), as Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 72, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1820);
